    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "The region $R$ is bounded by the curve $y=\\tan x$, the $x$-axis and the vertical line $x=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$. Show that $R$ has area $\\ln 2$ square units.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\ln 2$ square units.",
      "worked": "On $0\\le x\\le\\frac{\\pi}{3}$, the curve lies on or above the $x$-axis and meets it at $x=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nA&=\\int_0^{\\pi/3}\\tan x\\,dx\\\\\nA&=\\left[-\\ln(\\cos x)\\right]_0^{\\pi/3}\\\\\nA&=-\\ln\\left(\\frac12\\right)+\\ln 1\\\\\nA&=\\ln 2\\text{ square units}.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 23
  },
